<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Theme system</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as themes</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The theme system was the military and administrative organisation of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantine Empire</a> from around the seventh century, in which provinces called themes were governed by military commanders. Soldiers were supported by grants of land in return for hereditary military service. Accounts of the Byzantine Empire treat the themes as central to the empire's survival, linking defence, taxation and rural society.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/theme-system.jpg" alt="Theme system" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Professor Gustav Droysen (Hg.), Professor G. Hertzberg (Zeichnung) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Droysen_-_Ostr%C3%B6misches_Reich.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
